From 05955402d1bbe17801c758d604ffd04eb1135c47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Swapnil Raj <raj.swapnil99@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 16:20:19 +0000
Subject: feat: add Blake3 compress inner precompile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the Blake3 compress_inner syscall as a first-class SP1
precompile, enabling efficient ZK-proven Blake3 hashing.

- Guest stub: syscalls/blake3_compress.rs (ecall via BLAKE3_COMPRESS_INNER)
- Minimal executor: natively computes compress_inner and writes state back
- Tracing executor: records memory access events and state_out
- Event: Blake3CompressEvent with state_in/out, msg, memory records
- Machine chip (Blake3CompressChip): 104 rows/invocation
  - 16 state_init + 16 msg_read + 56 compute (one G call/row) + 16 finalize
  - AIR constraints for G function steps (Add, XOR, RotR 16/12/8/7)
  - Blake3Compress interaction bus chains rows 0→103→controller
- Controller chip (Blake3CompressControlChip): 1 row/invocation
  - Sends interaction at index=0 with initial state + msg
  - Receives interaction at index=104 with final state
- SyscallCode: BLAKE3_COMPRESS_INNER = 0x00_01_01_34
- RiscvAirId: Blake3Compress = 73, Blake3CompressControl = 74
- InteractionKind: Blake3Compress = 22
- Test: proves guest program and verifies output matches reference impl

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
